  Reel script says the Padi Pooja 'took place' (நடைபெற்றது) and the caption lists it as held, but the article's key point is the event's account; this is consistent, so no issue there.
  Reel script and caption say the 18 gold steps were decorated with flowers and a lamp lit 'in the evening', which matches the article, but the article says the Karthigai month Padi Pooja started with Ganapathi Homam 'the day before yesterday morning' while the reel script attributes that timing to 'நேற்று முன்தினம்' consistently — no issue.
  Slide 3 and caption state that the Padi Pooja is held on the 5th Tamil month date and the darshan opens on the 1st; the article says 'தமிழ் மாதம், 1ல்' and 'தமிழ் மாதம், 5ல்' which matches, but the caption adds 'ஒவ்வொரு' (every), which is an added detail not in the article.
  Slide 1 hl2 and slide 2 state 'திரளான பக்தர்கள் பங்கேற்பு'; the article says 'திரளானோர்' (large crowd) without specifying devotees, a minor wording addition.
  Caption describes the temple as 'கேரளா ஐயப்பன் கோவில் வடிவில்' which matches the article's form, but the reel script's sentence 'கோவிலில் நம்பூதிரிகள் பாரம்பரிய முறையில் பூஜைகள் செய்கின்றனர்' is grammatically awkward mixing the Namboothiri detail with the timing claims, making it two facts in one sentence.
  The reel script mentions 'நேற்று முன்தினம்' while the article's phrase is in a dated context; the posting date is today, so the reference is relative to the article's date and may be inaccurate for viewers.
